+The prepared value is deliberately not itself a `KernelBuildSpec` or cache
+key. Its exact callable ABI and canonical source allow the existing finalizer
+to construct the complete key without device-code assembly. The compiler does
+not invent a provisional digest, rewrite a key after publication, or run phase
+one again after lookup. Warm lookup avoids `tileiras`; it does not avoid HIR
+validation, TensorIR lowering, or exact ABI preparation.
+
+There is currently no per-key build lock. Concurrent processes that miss the
+same key may both assemble; atomic no-replace publication selects one identical
+winner. This is why no wait-hit disposition is exposed. Single-flight/per-key
+locking remains a separate availability and efficiency improvement.
 
